### Peridial Minting — Credential and Account Integrity, Card Conduit Generator & Blockchain

This extends CBBC v0.4 — Crypto Synchronous Bounded Autonomy into a credential issuance and documentary-preservation subsystem.

The central concept is a controlled process that transforms an authorized account credential into a verifiable digital identity record, generates a corresponding Card Conduit, and anchors its issuance and lifecycle history to a blockchain-backed integrity ledger.

Core principle: A credential may be minted, renewed, transferred under authorization, suspended, or revoked—but its provenance and audit history must remain verifiable.

### 1\. System definition

Peridial Minting is a proposed cryptographic credential lifecycle architecture connecting five functions:

* Credential Integrity — establish the authenticity and status of a credential.

* Account Integrity — bind the credential to an authorized account without exposing unnecessary personal information.

* Card Conduit Generator (CCG) — create a structured, machine-readable and human-readable credential conduit.

* Blockchain Anchoring — preserve verifiable issuance, authorization, and lifecycle events.

* Peridial Synchronization — associate credential recognition with an independently verifiable clock profile and synchronization record.

